  "body": "What changed:\n- The Browser View door has a new box, \"Show work envelope\". It is off by default. It is disabled when no machine is mounted on the active setup.\n- With a machine mounted, the viewport draws an outline of the tool-tip travel volume. A mill, mill-turn, plasma or EDM machine gets a box. A lathe gets a cylinder on the spindle axis.\n- The figures are the same travel, axis direction and work origin that the program stroke check reads. The picture cannot disagree with a refusal.\n- A machine without travel draws nothing. The tooltip names the missing figure.\n- The box is view state, like \"Show world origin axes\". It queues no command, is not saved and does not change posting or any check. No MCP tool is needed for display state.\n- Pure shape maths: `crates/post/src/machine/envelope.rs`. World glue: `crates/app/src/machine/work_envelope.rs`. UI: `crates/ui/src/work_envelope.rs`.\n\nDecisions (`docs/decisions/1567-work-envelope.md`):\n- The envelope is measured from the work origin, not from a table. No machine file states a table position, so the \"sits on the floor\" placement is not drawn. The tooltip says so.\n- Outline only. Faint faces need a new GPU path, so they are left out of this slice.\n\nPinning tests:\n- `machine::envelope::tests` (camcraft-post lib): box, inverted axis, missing travel, lathe cylinder.\n- `egui_app::tests::work_envelope` (camcraft-ui lib): disabled without a machine, box drawn and toggle is view state (no pending command, no history entry, machine unchanged), no travel gives a reason.\n\nQuick gate: green (post, app and ui suites), clippy `-D warnings` clean on post, app and ui.\n\nNot exercised: the GUI was not launched. The test does not post G-code to compare output. It shows that the machine and the history do not change, and the new code never reads the post. The mill-on-table floor, rotary reach and the faint faces are not drawn.\n\nChangelog: The Browser View door shows the machine's work envelope as an outline (#1567, PR #1786)\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: no\n\nFixes #1567\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
